des to \"needs_operator\". Never let the only headline field be the absence of an answer.","severity":"critical"},{"claim":"A real failure is invisible in the summary. Event sequence 11 records flaky_check outcome=retryable_failure reason=tool_exited_non_zero, yet status shows failed:0, untriagedInterruptions:[], and no attentionReason mentioning flaky_check. Only a full event-tail read (50 events, ~15k tokens) surfaces it. An operator who glances goes back to sleep on a run that already broke.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Surface retry/failure state in the summary: add a retrying/degraded bucket to nodeStateCounts, and add an attentionReason for any node with a recorded non-success outcome since last triage, even when the runtime intends to retry.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"Silence detection is disabled for exactly the node that is stuck. judge has been state=running with no event for 103 observed silence seconds, and the sole reason attention is unknown is that judge has no_declared_budget. The one signal that would say \"hung, wake up\" is switched off precisely where it is needed.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Apply a default silence budget (per-profile or execution-wide fallback) when a node declares none, and report silence against that default rather than refusing to evaluate. Treat missing budget as a config warning, not as a reason to suppress the health verdict.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"The prescribed remedy is not reachable from the operator's surface. Every attentionReason points to remedy=\"declareNodeBudget\", but the exposed MCP tools (status, events, probe, routes, start, signal, approve, pause, resume, cancel, wake_arm, wake_status, wake_wait) contain no budget-declaring operation. The monitor tells the operator to do something the monitor cannot do.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Either expose a declareNodeBudget mutation on the same surface, or emit remedies as executable references (tool name + arguments) and validate at build time that every remedy string maps to a callable tool.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"Retry state carries no schedule. flaky_check sits in queued after a retryable_failure with no attempt count, no backoff, and no next-attempt timestamp in status or in the event payload. The operator cannot distinguish \"will retry in 5s\" from \"wedged forever\", which is the exact discrimination the sleep decision needs.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Include attempt number, max attempts, and nextAttemptAt on retryable_failure events and mirror them in status per node.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"The wake path gave no usable signal for the sleep loop. wake_arm at cursor 13 followed by wake_wait returned outcome=timeout after 60s while the run was silently stalled, so the block expired with the operator no better informed and no distinction between \"quiet because healthy\" and \"quiet because stuck\".","evidence":[],"remediation":"Let the lease ring on derived attention transitions (e.g. silence budget exceeded, node entered retry) in addition to log appends, so a stall wakes the operator instead of expiring the wait.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"Arming a lease perturbs the progress counter the operator reasons with: wake_arm returned headSequence 14 while contentHead stayed 13, so a read-only monitoring action advances the sequence an operator uses as a proxy for \"did anything happen\".","evidence":[],"remediation":"Keep lease bookkeeping off the content stream, or have status report contentHead alongside headSequence so a bumped sequence is not mistaken for progress.","severity":"low"},{"claim":"The status payload is not glanceable: ~20 top-level fields, no one-line verdict, and attentionReasons duplicates silenceUnevaluated verbatim, forcing the operator to parse redundant nested structures at 3am.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Add a single headline field (verdict + short human sentence) at the top of the payload, and drop one of the two identical reason arrays.","severity":"low"}],"gateId":"judge-usefulness","nodeId":"judge","passed":false},"type":"gate_verdict"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-19T00:37:38.969490300Z","previousHash":"sha256:6ef96b0688085ddae0b0ee58e1313f65272a906e47743f2affe565d518961671","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge7","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":16,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge7"}],"evidenceIds":["exec-exec-m08-judge7-judge-a1-judgment"],"expectedNextSequence":15,"formatVersion":"1.0.0","requestDigest":"sha256:16785eb8be06cbdc44432294d89a6c7fa6d0dd3bd09f261598bd036f998841fe","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge7","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"streamId":"exec-m08-judge7"}
